  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Between October 2020 and November 2021, the National Trade Union Centre of Trinidad and Tobago (NATUC) partnered with Cipriani College of Labour &amp; Co-operative Studies (CCLCS) to mainstream the fight against gender based violence in all the services they provide. 
1) Increased capacity of workers&apos; representatives to negotiate inclusion of protections for workers victims of GBV during the negotiation process and prepared a cadre of trained personnel with knowledge of and the capacity to negotiate and implement the sexual exploitation and abuse (SEA) procedure (following UN guidelines). (A series of 5 workshops in December 2020 and February, March and June 2021).
2) NATUC has negotiated inclusion of protections for workers victims of gender based violence.
3) In November 2021, NATUC developed several tools and policies on Gender-Based Violence (GBV) that protects and supports the vulnerable at the workplace. This include:
-  model frameworks, templates, reporting mechanisms and clear procedures that address gender-based discrimination at the workplace;
- a model process and template for the investigation of allegations of sexual exploitation and abuse at the workplace.
This was supported by a media campaign that raised awareness of the trade union members and general public on the GBV.
 In line with the union&apos;s Strategic Plan 2020-2025, focusing on providing better services to its members through education and training, from February 22 till May 21, 2021 Transport &amp; Industrial Workers Union (TIWU) in order to enhance the training and negotiating capacity of the union conducted a series of training sessions for 11 shop stewards and central committee members. As a result the union has developed a cadre of personnel with capacity to participate in collective bargaining, provide advice to members on social protection, occupational safety and health, organising strategies, effective communications. ILO supported NATUC to become implementing partner to the Spotlight Initiative to Eliminate Violence Against Women and girls and provided technical advice on the development and implementation of the trade-union focused activities. 
ILO supported the development and implementation of training programme for TIWU. ILO specialists participated as resource persons.</narrative>
   </description>
